# deploy/local's engine image now builds from the repository root (D-012:
# a context of engine/ alone left ~90 of the engine's own tests unable to
# find the repo-root files they read by design). This file is what keeps
# that build from also copying in everything the .gitignore excludes plus
# the local caches nothing in a fresh checkout should have anyway.
#
# .git/ is deliberately NOT excluded here, even though it is repository
# history rather than source: business_map.py, release_check.py, runs.py
# and state_map.py all shell out to `git` and need real history present to
# answer (business_map.py's day-count-since-first-commit in particular).
# Excluding it was the first version of this file and cost a build — the
# baked test run failed a second time, narrower, on exactly the tests that
# needed it. node_modules/ and .next/ are the two heaviest directories in
# this repository (519 MB and 17 MB measured here) and neither the engine
# image nor its test suite touches either.

node_modules/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python — every interpreter's own venv and bytecode cache, never a build
# input. engine/.venv/ was 91 MB measured here and was never excluded by
# name before this file existed.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Secrets and local generated output — mirrors .gitignore. A build input
# is not the place a credential should be reachable from even if it never
# ends up in a layer; refusing to look is cheaper than checking after.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
.n8n/
.searxng/
.hfcache/
.insightface/
packs/*/images/
packs/ambassador-out/
packs/flux-out/
packs/flux-v2/
packs/flux-faces/
packs/*.zip
packs/*.log

.DS_Store
.vercel
